	(text "## About ESP32-C3 pins\n\n### Boot pins\n\nGPIO 2, GPIO 8, GPIO 9 must be HIGH at boot / startup.\nSince the boolean blocks pull the pin up to 3.3V,\nthey should be safe to use.\n\nIf the pin is not populated,\nthe pin is pulled up internally.\n\n### ADC2 PIN\n\nGPIO 5 is reserved for WIFI (ADC2)\nand can't be used for signal sampling.\n\nUsing it for boolean input or output should be fine.\n\n### USB pins (GPIO18, GPIO19)\n\nGPIO 18, GPIO 19 are used for USB communication.\n\n### ADC1 pins\n\nGPIO 0, 1, 3, 4 have access to ADC1.\nADC1 is free to use!\nUse them for signal inputs.\n\n### Actually general purpose input output pins\n\nGPIO 6, 7, 10 don't have access to ADC,\nso use them for anything except signal input.\n\nIn ESP32, any pin has access to PWM (signal output),\nbut only 6 PWM channels can coexist at the same time.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 99.06 63.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9b48e8b7-0bc1-4b0f-943c-8426a73fc024")
	)
	(text "## Pin layout\n\nGPIO 0: signal_in\nGPIO 1: signal_in\nGPIO 2: bool_in\nGPIO 3: signal_out\nGPIO 4: signal_out\nGPIO 5: bool_in\nGPIO 6: bool_out\nGPIO 7: bool_in\nGPIO 8: bool_in\nGPIO 9: bool_out\nGPIO 10:bool_out"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 145.542 62.992 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.762 0.762)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f892fca9-22fd-428e-8af6-d03ccfea5f5e")
	)
